  "reference": "ffmpeg-transport-views-native",
  "contract": [
    "Use Reader with the access-unit contract’s audio and subtitle tail reporting and explicit ADTS and LATM policies. Read its track views through TrackInfo.",
    "Read the complete mpegts-access-units corpus through the selected program, advancing ordered entities and flushing at a declared discontinuity. The reference uses the public parser-enabled MPEG-TS demuxer with NOFILLIN, without stream discovery.",
    "The packet record compares stream index, PID, demux PTS and DTS, duration, position, flags, payload length and bytes, and time base. A following record compares each side-data element in order. Clean end requires consuming the last physical entity.",
    "Compare the media kind, codec identity, native tag, configuration epoch and codec configuration bytes for each track. The reference observes AVProgram.pmt_version and AVStream.codecpar, giving the first visible PMT epoch number 2.",
    "Compare the AC-3 and E-AC-3 syncframe lengths with the public AC-3 parser applied to the reference packet. For DVB subtitles, count EN 300 743 §7.2 segments and compare the leftover truncated extent. For opaque video and private audio, compare the reported elementary range against the reference packet payload extent and compare private audio carriage from the codec and transport tag."
  ],
